> - Seven escapes, and no others: `\n` `\t` `\r` `\\` `\"` and `\u{...}`, a code
>   point in hex that is not 0 or a surrogate (`\u{e9}` is `é`), in a string,
>   `\'` instead of `\"` in a character literal. Any other escape is a compile
>   error.
